`)}const Tg={id:"delight",label:"delight-driven (people buy this because they want it)",demand:"Demand is proven by an EXISTING BUDGET for the same appetite plus evidence of REPEAT engagement — what these people already pay monthly to be entertained, informed or absorbed, and whether they come back. It is NOT proven by an acute problem, because there usually is not one.",problem:"Do NOT demand an acute pain, and do NOT accept an invented one. The honest gate-2 answer here is the RECURRING APPETITE: what the buyer already does for this feeling, how often, and what they already spend on it. 'Boredom with the passive version of this' is a legitimate answer; a manufactured ache is not. Treat a dramatic pain statement on a delight product as a WARNING SIGN of over-claiming, not as strength.",money:"A purchase alone is WEAK evidence here — novelty converts exactly once. A credible test pairs the money with a depth-or-return signal: did they finish, did they come back, did they go deeper unprompted. Money plus engagement is the pass; money alone is a fun toy that gets used twice.",trap:"The characteristic death is DELIGHT DECAY: strong first session, no second one. Hunt for whether anything in the offer earns a return visit, and whether the novelty is the product or merely the packaging."},Ig={id:"regulated",label:"regulated / high-trust (the buyer carries liability)",demand:"Demand is proven by budget that already moves through a procurement or compliance line, and by who carries the risk if this goes wrong. Enthusiasm from a user who cannot sign is not demand.",problem:"The pain is real but it is usually RISK, COST OF ERROR or OBLIGATION, not inconvenience. Demand that the problem name the consequence of getting it wrong, and be explicit about whether the user and the buyer are the same person — they very often are not.",money:"A credible test names the person who can actually authorise spend and what they need before they can. A pilot, a signed LOI, or a paid trial counts; enthusiasm from a non-signer does not.",trap:"The characteristic death is a delighted user who cannot buy, and a procurement or compliance path nobody costed. Hunt for the approval chain and the liability question."},Og={id:"operational",label:"pain-driven (people buy this to stop something hurting)",demand:"Demand is proven by an acute, frequent, expensive problem the buyer is already spending money or hours on — workarounds, spreadsheets, staff time, or a competing tool they resent paying for.",problem:"Demand the pain in the buyer's own words, with its frequency and its cost. Vague dissatisfaction is not a problem; a named, recurring, quantifiable loss is.",money:"A credible test extracts real money or a signed commitment against the promise of relief — a deposit, a prepay, a paid pilot. Interest is not validation.",trap:"The characteristic death is a problem that is real but not expensive enough to act on — a vitamin sold as a painkiller. Hunt for whether anyone is currently paying anything to solve it."},Hx=/entertain|media|game|gaming|interactive|consumer app|creator|arts|culture|music|film|tv|travel|leisure|sport|recreation|food|drink|hobby|toy|fashion|social|dating|fitness|wellness|edutainment|consumer learning|lifelong learning/i,qx=/health|clinic|medical|pharma|finance|fintech|bank|insur|legal|law|compliance|government|public sector|school|university|k-12|campus|district|childcare|aviation|energy|utilit/i;function Vx(e,t){const n=(e??"").trim();if(!n)return null;const r=Gx[String(t??"").trim()];return r||(Hx.test(n)?Tg:qx.test(n)?Ig:Og)}const Gx={delight:Tg,regulated:Ig,operational:Og},md=[{id:"delight",when:"People buy it because they WANT it — entertainment, hobbies, identity, curiosity, comfort. There is usually no acute pain, and demand shows up as existing spend plus repeat engagement."},{id:"regulated",when:"Someone carries LIABILITY or the money moves through procurement/compliance — healthcare, finance, legal, schools, aviation, government. The user and the buyer are often different people."},{id:"operational",when:"A business buys it to relieve a concrete operating pain — cost, time, error, risk to the work itself. Demand shows up as budget already being spent on the problem."}];function Wx(e,t){const n=Vx(e,t);return n?`

